#. type: Title #
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using Yii with Rapira"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Rapira](https://rapira.rs/) is a PHP application server written in Rust that embeds the PHP interpreter.\n"
"The [Yii Rapira runner](https://github.com/yiisoft/yii-runner-rapira) supports its classic, worker, and dispatcher modes.\n"
"Worker and dispatcher modes initialize the application once per worker and reuse it for subsequent requests.\n"
"See [Using Yii with event loop](using-with-event-loop.md) for the implications of keeping the application in memory.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"The runner requires PHP 8.4–8.5. Install the Rapira binary following the "
"[Rapira installation instructions](https://rapira.rs/docs/intro/"
"installation), using a PHP version supported by the runner.  The Composer "
"packages provide the Yii integration; the server binary must be installed "
"separately."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid "Install the runner and its contract package in your Yii application:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (shell)
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "composer require yiisoft/yii-runner-rapira:@dev rapira/contract:@dev\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"These stability flags allow the development versions used by the runner's "
"installation instructions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"The following example assumes an application based on `yiisoft/app` or "
"`yiisoft/app-api`, with `App\\Environment` and `src/bootstrap.php` provided "
"by the template."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid "Create `worker.php` in the application root:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (php)
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<?php\n"
"\n"
"declare(strict_types=1);\n"
"\n"
"use App\\Environment;\n"
"use Psr\\Log\\LogLevel;\n"
"use Yiisoft\\ErrorHandler\\ErrorHandler;\n"
"use Yiisoft\\ErrorHandler\\Renderer\\PlainTextRenderer;\n"
"use Yiisoft\\Log\\Logger;\n"
"use Yiisoft\\Log\\StreamTarget;\n"
"use Yiisoft\\Yii\\Runner\\Rapira\\RapiraApplicationRunner;\n"
"\n"
"$root = __DIR__;\n"
"\n"
"require_once $root . '/src/bootstrap.php';\n"
"\n"
"$runner = new RapiraApplicationRunner(\n"
"    rootPath: $root,\n"
"    debug: Environment::appDebug(),\n"
"    checkEvents: Environment::appDebug(),\n"
"    environment: Environment::appEnv(),\n"
"    temporaryErrorHandler: new ErrorHandler(\n"
"        new Logger(\n"
"            [\n"
"                (new StreamTarget())->setLevels([\n"
"                    LogLevel::EMERGENCY,\n"
"                    LogLevel::ERROR,\n"
"                    LogLevel::WARNING,\n"
"                ]),\n"
"            ],\n"
"        ),\n"
"        new PlainTextRenderer(),\n"
"    ),\n"
");\n"
"$runner->run();\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"The runner creates the container, starts the application, converts incoming "
"requests to PSR-7 requests, and emits responses. It detects the Rapira "
"execution mode, so the same entry script can be used with all three modes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid "Create `rapira.toml` next to `worker.php`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (toml)
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[http]\n"
"listen = \"127.0.0.1:8000\"\n"
"\n"
"[pool]\n"
"entrypoint = \"worker.php\"\n"
"mode = \"worker\"\n"
"max_requests = 1000\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"This configuration listens on the loopback interface and recycles each "
"worker after 1,000 requests.  For serving files from `public`, follow "
"Rapira's [static file configuration](https://rapira.rs/docs/static-files).  "
"See the [configuration reference](https://rapira.rs/docs/configuration) for "
"the other server and pool settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid "Run the following command from the application root:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (shell)
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "rapira serve\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"Open `http://127.0.0.1:8000` to access the application. Restart the server "
"after changing application code or configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution modes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"Set `mode` in the `[pool]` section of `rapira.toml` to choose how requests "
"are processed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"`classic` initializes the application for each request, similarly to PHP-FPM."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"`worker` keeps the application in memory and receives requests through PHP's "
"SAPI superglobals."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"`dispatcher` keeps the application in memory and receives request objects "
"through Rapira's dispatcher API.  The Yii runner processes these requests "
"sequentially within each worker."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"See [Rapira execution modes](https://rapira.rs/docs/execution-modes) for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"In worker and dispatcher modes, services may retain state between requests. "
"The runner calls `Yiisoft\\Di\\StateResetter::reset()` after each request, "
"but you must configure resetters for your own stateful services.  See the "
"[Yii DI documentation](https://github.com/yiisoft/di#resetting-services-"
"state)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"The `max_requests` setting limits how long a worker lives; it does not "
"replace resetting request-specific state."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/guide/tutorial/using-yii-with-rapira.md
msgid ""
"`RapiraApplicationRunner` uses the application templates' web configuration "
"groups by default. Its constructor accepts alternative groups, configuration "
"directories, and a temporary error handler. Use `withConfig()` to supply a "
"custom configuration instance or `withContainer()` to supply a PSR-11 "
"container. See the [runner documentation](https://github.com/yiisoft/yii-"
"runner-rapira#configuration) for examples."
msgstr ""
